in Bash, string quoting constructs are syntactic 
mechanisms that control how strings are interpreted
 — especially how special characters, variables,
 command substitutions, and escape sequences behave.

These constructs tell the shell whether it should interpret 
or treat certain characters literally. The quoting behavior is tightly
tied to how Bash parses commands and expands words during lexical analysis 
and parameter expansion.

1 tokenizer. 
2 lexer
3 linked list
[ ]->[ ]->[ ]

[echo] [hh hh] [tt tt]
[echohh hhtt] [tt]